{
  "0": "Reduce causal context length to 64 interactions in training, validation and prediction, retaining chronological order and existing padding. Shorter histories may reduce stale-interest interference and recurrent computation within the trial allowance. Preserve embeddings, GRU topology, readout, loss and optimizer; persist maxlen in metadata and keep the predictor writer consistent.",
  "1": "Add a fixed residual path out = gru_out + 0.1 * dropped_input_embedding at every nonpadding position, identically in forward and encode. This may preserve recent item identity while the GRU learns sequential corrections, with little added computation. Keep GRU depth, embeddings, scoring, history selection, readout, loss and optimizer unchanged; reproduce the architecture through the predictor writer.",
  "2": "Untie input and candidate item embeddings: retain the existing table for GRU inputs and introduce one output table shared by positive, negative and candidate scoring. Initialize the output table by copying the initial input weights, then train both jointly within one model per dataset. Separating contextual and retrieval roles may reduce conflicting gradients. Preserve dimensions, dot-product scoring, GRU, history policy, loss and optimizer; update checkpoint loading and the predictor writer.",
  "3": "Reduce training batch size from 128 to 64 while retaining the existing number of batches per epoch, Adam settings, cosine scheduler, dropout, validation cadence, stopping rule and 200-epoch cap. Smaller batches may regularize through noisier gradients while reducing computation and memory after the recent timeout. Preserve seed 42, architecture, features, scoring, readout, loss and all four dataset routes."
